WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:06.301
Marius had lived in poverty for several years, but he had never known true desperation.

2
00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:13.380
He had seen true desperation in the form of this girl—this phantom—who had just passed before his eyes.

3
00:00:13.381 --> 00:00:18.213
She had revealed to him an entirely new and hideous kind of poverty.

4
00:00:18.214 --> 00:00:28.183
She and her family had fallen so low, become so poor, that they could only be described as people living in misery— les

5
00:00:28.184 --> 00:00:36.429
misérables . Every day before her visit, Marius must have seen the girl, or a member of her family, in the hall of the

6
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.349
Gorbeau house. He could hear their voices through the thin wall that separated their apartment

7
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:47.270
from his. But he had never paid attention. Yes, he had paid their rent, but anyone would have

8
00:00:47.271 --> 00:00:51.430
done that. A better neighbor would have paid attention to them and done more

9
00:00:51.431 --> 00:00:56.454
for them. Suddenly Marius noticed a small hole that he had never

10
00:00:56.455 --> 00:01:00.922
seen before. It was near the ceiling on the wall that divided the

11
00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:05.790
two apartments. "Let’s see what this Jondrette family is like," said Marius as he climbed on

12
00:01:05.791 --> 00:01:09.660
a table. "It’s not wrong to spy on people if your intention is to

13
00:01:09.661 --> 00:01:15.906
help them." Marius looked through the hole. His room was badly furnished, but at least it

14
00:01:15.907 --> 00:01:18.438
was clean. The room next door

15
00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:26.074
was filthy. The furniture consisted of a cane chair, a rickety table, and two dirty beds on either side of

16
00:01:26.075 --> 00:01:32.463
the fireplace. The dark corners of this room hid who knows what—perhaps spiders as big as

17
00:01:32.464 --> 00:01:40.892
one’s fist. A man with a long gray beard sat smoking at a table. He was writing, probably a letter such as the ones Marius

18
00:01:40.893 --> 00:01:48.384
had read. He was wearing a woman’s blouse over a pair of muddy trousers. His toes stuck out from his broken-down

19
00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:53.122
boots. A large woman with graying red hair squatted near the

20
00:01:53.123 --> 00:02:02.447
fireplace. She too was wearing a blouse, but hers was worn with a patched skirt. Marius could see a girl lying listlessly on one of the

21
00:02:02.448 --> 00:02:06.360
beds. Probably the younger sister of the girl who had visited

22
00:02:06.361 --> 00:02:14.424
him. Marius was about to step away from his spy hole when the door to the neighbors’ apartment opened and the elder daughter

23
00:02:14.425 --> 00:02:19.186
appeared. Wrapped in a ragged old gown, she was wearing men’s work

24
00:02:19.187 --> 00:02:23.670
boots. She was breathless and yet there was a triumphant look on her

25
00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:30.749
face. "He’s coming!" she announced. "I found him at the Church of Saint Jacques du Haut

26
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.234
Pas." "The generous man?" asked Monsieur

27
00:02:34.235 --> 00:02:43.559
Jondrette. "Yes, he said his daughter had to make some purchases, but he would be along soon. I tell you he’s coming

28
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.669
now." "Wife, put out the

29
00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:52.901
fire!" The surprised woman did not stir, so her husband grabbed a broken pot on the mantel and threw water on the

30
00:02:52.902 --> 00:02:58.559
fire. Then, turning to his elder daughter, he said, "Break the

31
00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.154
chair!" "What do you mean?" she

32
00:03:01.155 --> 00:03:06.980
asked. He seized the chair and kicked out the cane seat. "Is it cold outside?" he asked

33
00:03:06.981 --> 00:03:09.972
her. "Very cold and it’s

34
00:03:09.973 --> 00:03:16.384
snowing." The father turned toward the younger girl on the bed. "Get up, you good-for-nothing, and break a

35
00:03:16.385 --> 00:03:21.868
windowpane." The girl sprang off the bed, trembling. She was speechless at his

36
00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:28.384
command. "Did you hear me?" roared Monsieur Jondrette. "I told you to break a

37
00:03:28.385 --> 00:03:35.471
windowpane." The girl, with a sort of terrified obedience, rose up on tiptoe and smashed the window with her

38
00:03:35.472 --> 00:03:38.360
fist. The glass broke and fell with a

39
00:03:38.361 --> 00:03:44.289
crash. "Good," said the father. He ran his eyes over all the nooks and crannies of the

40
00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:48.789
room. He was like a general making his final preparations before the

41
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:55.931
battle. Madame Jondrette slowly got up and asked, "Dear, what do you want me to

42
00:03:55.932 --> 00:04:04.439
do?" "Get into bed." His tone of voice showed he tolerated no disobedience. The mother threw herself heavily onto a

43
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.510
bed. Meanwhile the younger daughter was

44
00:04:07.511 --> 00:04:10.756
sobbing. "What’s wrong with you?" asked the

45
00:04:10.757 --> 00:04:16.685
father. She showed him her bleeding fist. In breaking the window, she had cut

46
00:04:16.686 --> 00:04:22.415
herself. It was the mother’s turn to scold her husband. "See what a stupid thing you’ve

47
00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:26.185
done! You told her to break the glass, and she’s hurt

48
00:04:26.186 --> 00:04:30.828
herself." "So much the better! Now she looks even more

49
00:04:30.829 --> 00:04:36.074
pitiful." Monsieur Jondrette tore a strip from his blouse and wound it around his daughter’s

50
00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:42.979
hand. An icy wind blew through the broken window. The father looked around to be sure he hadn’t forgotten

51
00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:48.891
anything. "I think we’re ready to receive the generous man from the

52
00:04:48.892 --> 00:04:57.050
church." Just then there was a knock at the door. Monsieur Jondrette rushed forward and opened it with many low bows and

53
00:04:57.051 --> 00:05:05.479
smiles. "Ah, my benefactor!" he exclaimed. "Please come in and bring your lovely daughter with

54
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:09.050
you." A man with white hair and a girl walked into the

55
00:05:09.051 --> 00:05:14.971
room. Marius, who had been watching all this, almost fell from his perch in

56
00:05:14.972 --> 00:05:21.709
surprise. It was Ursula—the radiant young woman who had been the object of his adoration in the Luxembourg

57
00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:30.288
Gardens! She looked just the same, perhaps a little paler. She was wearing a black cloak trimmed with fur and a violet velvet

58
00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:35.772
hat. Below her long dress, Marius caught a glimpse of her tiny foot in a satin

59
00:05:35.773 --> 00:05:44.836
shoe. The elder Jondrette daughter was also taking in the girl’s outfit and her charming, happy face, but with a look of evil

60
00:05:44.837 --> 00:05:48.423
intent. The girl laid a large package on the table.

61
00:05:48.424 --> 00:05:55.773
"Monsieur, you’ll find here some new clothes, warm stockings, and blankets," said Monsieur Leblanc.

62
00:05:55.774 --> 00:06:02.090
"Our angelic benefactor overwhelms us," Monsieur Jondrette said loudly.

63
00:06:02.091 --> 00:06:10.765
To his older daughter he whispered, "I don’t want clothes and blankets! I want money! Which letter did you give him?"

64
00:06:10.766 --> 00:06:14.461
"The one signed Fabantou," she whispered back.

65
00:06:14.462 --> 00:06:17.669
"Right, the actor. Good."

66
00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:23.082
"I see that you are indeed to be pitied," said Monsieur Leblanc, looking around the room.

67
00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:31.987
"Yes, look. My poor darlings have no bread and no fire. The window is broken and in such weather as this!

68
00:06:31.988 --> 00:06:37.471
My wife is sick, and my child is injured. Look at her bleeding wrist.

69
00:06:37.472 --> 00:06:41.714
It was an accident at the factory where she earns only a few coins a week.

70
00:06:41.715 --> 00:06:48.130
I fear the doctor may have to cut off her arm—if we can even afford a doctor."

71
00:06:48.131 --> 00:06:53.050
"Indeed!" said Monsieur Leblanc, clearly alarmed by the situation.

72
00:06:53.051 --> 00:06:59.717
The girl, who believed that she might now lose her arm, began to sob. But her father paid no attention.

73
00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:06.630
He was busy looking at the generous man because there was something familiar about that man.

74
00:07:06.631 --> 00:07:13.614
"The rent is due in a few days," Jondrette went on. "I owe sixty francs."

75
00:07:13.615 --> 00:07:19.490
Monsieur Leblanc drew five francs from his pocket. "That’s all I have right now.

76
00:07:19.491 --> 00:07:26.781
I must take my daughter home, but I’ll bring you sixty francs tonight. And here—take my coat."

77
00:07:26.782 --> 00:07:30.266
Monsieur Jondrette escorted the Leblancs downstairs.

78
00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:35.606
Marius was desperate to learn where they lived, but he couldn’t let the father catch sight of him.

79
00:07:35.607 --> 00:07:39.507
He followed them downstairs and saw them getting into a cab.

80
00:07:39.508 --> 00:07:43.194
Marius looked frantically for a cab but couldn’t find one.

81
00:07:43.195 --> 00:07:49.071
As their cab disappeared around the corner, he stood in the street and watched helplessly.

